  "notes": "Boot a Junk Yard ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released); the scenario names no game, so one byte-identical file serves every jy_* driver it is run against (jy_12, jy_11 and the jy_03 prototype). Navigate the service menu to T.1 SWITCH EDGES and start it, then drive each public edge separately, holding each level for 2 s: 45 (Ramp Exit, an ordinary switch), 41 (Past Spinner, a printed A-16908/A-16909 opto that jyGameData's inverted-switch mask normalizes) and 44 (Past Crane, the same printed opto pair, not normalized). The ROM's top display line names a switch while it reads it as active, so the edge that brings the name up shows which public level the ROM treats as active.",
